cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss Plectis, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "Plectis"
abstract: "A local Python toolkit that checks claims about software nobody watched being built. Point it at a project and it writes a record you can re-run: the route it took, the evidence behind each finding, and where that finding stops. The repository publishes the same mechanism as an executable reference corpus, each component carrying a typed evidence class, a local receipt, and an explicit authority ceiling. It runs entirely on your machine."
